    {
      "id": "kdxTbw2WsnT8TeI-RVe3R",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1352.4761904761933,
      "y": 135.6190476190476,
      "width": 710.7994995117188,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aZ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1465399646,
      "version": 698,
      "versionNonce": 1039966686,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786554409253,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Second approach\n- Containarized servers (stateless) \n- Load Balancer per region, as it is a distributed system it \nwill be a good choice \n- Now the server capabilities was improved\n- Single point of failure - Database\n- load balancer + server / region but the database still unique \n- CAP theorem. For distribuited system the P is required and we cannot \nhave the 3 options, just 3, here I will choose the C, CP. We need a\nconsistent and Partioned database. -> Postgres, ACID, CP",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Second approach\n- Containarized servers (stateless) \n- Load Balancer per region, as it is a distributed system it \nwill be a good choice \n- Now the server capabilities was improved\n- Single point of failure - Database\n- load balancer + server / region but the database still unique \n- CAP theorem. For distribuited system the P is required and we cannot \nhave the 3 options, just 3, here I will choose the C, CP. We need a\nconsistent and Partioned database. -> Postgres, ACID, CP",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
