    },
    {
      "id": "8n83zS6Iz523Sr8BYPEsk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2532.1428571428614,
      "y": 418.2857142857141,
      "width": 997.619384765625,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0l",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 252904642,
      "version": 639,
      "versionNonce": 1527054110,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786556036648,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Last approach\n- Containarized servers (stateless) \n- Load Balancer per region, as it is a distributed system it \nwill be a good choice \n - Sharded database + hash (id) %len(shard) . Now our app can write in multiples shard of the dabase\n - Snowflak id  \n - Redis with per region with the 20% most accessed regions \n - we dont need to hit the database to check if id exists (snowflake)\n- load balancer + server / region but the database still unique \n- CAP theorem. For distribuited system the P is required and we cannot \nhave the 3 options, just 3, here I will choose the C, CP. We need a\nconsistent and Partioned database. -> Postgres, ACID, CP\n- Rate limit per region(per shard)\n- WAF to avoid attacks",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Last approach\n- Containarized servers (stateless) \n- Load Balancer per region, as it is a distributed system it \nwill be a good choice \n - Sharded database + hash (id) %len(shard) . Now our app can write in multiples shard of the dabase\n - Snowflak id  \n - Redis with per region with the 20% most accessed regions \n - we dont need to hit the database to check if id exists (snowflake)\n- load balancer + server / region but the database still unique \n- CAP theorem. For distribuited system the P is required and we cannot \nhave the 3 options, just 3, here I will choose the C, CP. We need a\nconsistent and Partioned database. -> Postgres, ACID, CP\n- Rate limit per region(per shard)\n- WAF to avoid attacks",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
